cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Wiretap
message: If you use Wiretap in academic work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "theworker02"
    website: "https://github.com/theworker02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/theworker02/wiretap"
url: "https://github.com/theworker02/wiretap"
abstract: >-
  Wiretap is an offline, deterministic toolkit for evidence-backed binary
  protocol inference. It proposes competing field hypotheses with measured
  evidence, exports schemas and stubs, and refuses to invent confidence when
  evidence is insufficient. No LLM APIs; no telemetry.
keywords:
  - binary protocols
  - reverse engineering
  - protocol inference
  - offline analysis
  - kaitai
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.4.0"
